{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-29T05:11:32.568Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7f8557ee791cd266194a12fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-29T05:11:32.568Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Completed native admitted-write hardening: explicit SDK identities and revision-bound steps, deterministic peer identity adoption, per-invocation write counts, SDK semantic preview before any target application, source-based scope selection shared with legacy import, and configured-status filter normalization. Tests cover ordinary writers at inspection/capture/apply boundaries, keyed-creation races, peer edits during compensation, ABA replays, deleted targets, malformed retained bindings, all status roles and an empty executable PATH. Initial observation counts blank records toward its budget and remains non-authorizing at EOF. Public minimum SDK artifact 2026.8.20 has complete reads and status roles but lacks semantic preview and transaction-key derivation; read-only admission remains supported, while admitted application returns a typed upgrade remedy on such hosts. No dependency pin was changed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-29T05:11:32.568Z"}],"before_hash":"f58ba62d23eb497985497629bf187a45d82e96a7c79d827cb4f42218e1eb02c2","after_hash":"5526c34c64f78777d937c75bff40a43f04a0ca310a11c990e08a5c342619ebc8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_versi